From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 23:13:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] BD-J: without a security manager only in the isolated
 service, from Java 24

From Java 24 on there is no security manager, and Libbluray.init() failed
closed (BD-J did not start). In the isolated BD-J service the system
confines the disc's code instead, so there, and only where Java has none,
init() goes on without one: org.videolan.hades.sandboxed (set by bdj.c in
that process alone), Java 24 or later, and no manager in force. Anywhere
else it still fails closed. Java 8 to 17 keep the manager inside the
service too; shutdown() removes one only if there is one.

The security manager also did a job of its own: in files mode (the disc
reached through the player's file system, as Kodi gives it; discRoot null,
the VFS root is the cache) the read check of a file caches it from the disc
before anything opens it (BDJSecurityManager -> BDJLoader.accessFile()).
Without a manager no check happens and the disc's files are not there.
BDJLoader.accessFileWithoutSecurityManager() does the same as the check
(relative paths from the Xlet's home, canonical path, VFSCache.accessFile())
and is called where the check was: java.io.FileInputStream, and
java.io.BDFileSystem for File.exists() and the other attribute calls
(getBooleanAttributes(), getLength(), getLastModifiedTime(),
checkAccess()). Only in files mode (VFSCache.cachesAll()) and only without
a manager; with one, nothing changes.

Measured with OpenJDK 26 in the service and a BD-J disc made for the test,
opened through callbacks: the Xlet's File.exists() and FileInputStream of
BDMV/index.bdmv give true and 64 bytes; with the same jar without these
hooks, false and FileNotFoundException.

RandomAccessFile, java.nio.file and ZipFile do not go through these hooks;
a disc that opens a file of the disc that way, and not earlier through
File or FileInputStream, does not find it (not seen on a disc: not
verified).
